  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup all-purpose flour",
    "2 tablespoons white sugar",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "1 teaspoon baking soda",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "1.5 tablespoons butter",
    "2 cups whole wheat flour",
    "0.25 cup quick-cooking oatmeal",
    "1.5 cups nonfat plain yogurt",
    "1 teaspoon milk, or more as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Lightly grease a baking sheet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/LT_cqkf30qjFRPanlVNR2GLOE8o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-220525-irish-brown-bread-VAT-step-01-b1d1e43ec64f443891cf08421054fd30.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/220525/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix all-purpose flour, sugar, baking powder, baking soda, and salt together in a large bowl. Cut butter into flour mixture with a pastry blender or 2 knives until mixture forms fine crumbs. Stir in whole wheat flour and quick-cooking oatmeal until combined.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/E6qLxA4kHdHAym0ZtXOyfvZtXbo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-220525-irish-brown-bread-VAT-step-02-6ad99ebc0b9f4964b243deb648cbd09e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/220525/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gently stir in yogurt. If mixture is too dry to hold together, add milk, a little at a time, until dough holds together; it should not be too sticky.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/2UsKCyqdxIg5QoqY-xSlNELxkcQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-220525-irish-brown-bread-VAT-step-03-e3da9d93720a42d0826c33c0800d2954.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/220525/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn dough out onto a lightly floured work surface; knead gently about 5 times to form a ball. Place dough in the center of the prepared baking sheet; cut a large 'X' in the top of loaf.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JutYIZXCYEdGDdiX7NakUKxkkZY=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-220525-irish-brown-bread-VAT-step-04-d7020c3fa223443799592e1a6c155fe0.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/220525/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until well browned, about 40 minutes; transfer to a wire rack to cool. Bread can be served warm or cold.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/pFmvwoabMSaGqMYExjVcRqRVFdM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-220525-irish-brown-bread-VAT-step-05-aff25beefc9d43deadcc4175773a7172.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/220525/step_05.webp"
    }
  ],
